</div>
<div id="alg1.l11" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.l11.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">11:</span></span>
              
              
              <span id="alg1.l11.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">else</span> <span id="alg1.l11.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">if</span>  Diversity <math id="alg1.l11.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{V}(\mathcal{Q}_{\text{list}})&lt;\tau" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒬</mi><mtext>list</mtext></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{V}(\mathcal{Q}_{\text{list}})&lt;\tau</annotation></semantics></math> <span id="alg1.l11.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">then</span>



</div>
<div id="alg1.l12" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.l12.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">12:</span></span>
              
              
               Remove least contribution query in <math id="alg1.l12.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{V}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{V}</annotation></semantics></math> from <math id="alg1.l12.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{Q}_{\text{list}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒬</mi><mtext>list</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{Q}_{\text{list}}</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg1.l13" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.l13.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">13:</span></span>
              
              
              <span id="alg1.l13.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">else</span>


</div>
<div id="alg1.l14" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.l14.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">14:</span></span>
              
              
               Break

</div>
<div id="alg1.l15" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.l15.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">15:</span></span>
              
              
              <span id="alg1.l15.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">end</span> <span id="alg1.l15.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">if</span>
</div>
<div id="alg1.l16" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.l16.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">16:</span></span>
              
              
             <span id="alg1.l16.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">end</span> <span id="alg1.l16.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">for</span>
</div>
<div id="alg1.l17" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.l17.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">17:</span></span>
              
              
             <span id="alg1.l17.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">return</span> <math id="alg1.l17.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{Q}_{\text{list}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒬</mi><mtext>list</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{Q}_{\text{list}}</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
</div></div></div>
</figure>
</section>
<section id="S3.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">3.2 </span>Our Framework: CCCaption</h3>

<div id="S3.SS2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">To explicitly capture the two key aspects of caption, completeness and correctness, we propose the corresponding rewards to optimize <math id="S3.SS2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M_{\theta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>M</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M_{\theta}</annotation></semantics></math>. In addition, we introduce a dynamic query sampling strategy to improve training efficiency.</p>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS2.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S3.SS2.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.SS2.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Completeness Reward</span>.
We approximate the basic information set <math id="S3.SS2.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{B}_{\mathbf{x}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℬ</mi><mi>𝐱</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{B}_{\mathbf{x}}</annotation></semantics></math> by a set of visual queries
<math id="S3.SS2.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{Q}_{\mathbf{x}}\!=\!\{\mathbf{q}_{i}\}_{i=1}^{m}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒬</mi><mi>𝐱</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.108em" rspace="0.108em">=</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>𝐪</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>m</mi></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{Q}_{\mathbf{x}}\!=\!\{\mathbf{q}_{i}\}_{i=1}^{m}</annotation></semantics></math>, and reward captions that can answer more of these queries. Formally, the completeness reward is defined as</p>
<table id="S3.E4" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.E4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{R}_{\text{comp}}(\mathbf{x},\hat{\mathbf{y}})=\frac{1}{|\mathcal{Q}_{\mathbf{x}}|}\sum_{\mathbf{q}\in\mathcal{Q}_{\mathbf{x}}}\mathbb{I}\bigl(M_{J}(\hat{\mathbf{y}},\mathbf{q})\bigr)," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℛ</mi><mtext>comp</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>,</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐲</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒬</mi><mi>𝐱</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>𝐪</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒬</mi><mi>𝐱</mi></msub></mrow></munder><mrow><mi>𝕀</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>M</mi><mi>J</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐲</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>,</mo><mi>𝐪</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{R}_{\text{comp}}(\mathbf{x},\hat{\mathbf{y}})=\frac{1}{|\mathcal{Q}_{\mathbf{x}}|}\sum_{\mathbf{q}\in\mathcal{Q}_{\mathbf{x}}}\mathbb{I}\bigl(M_{J}(\hat{\mathbf{y}},\mathbf{q})\bigr),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(4)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.SS2.p2.2" class="ltx_p">where <math id="S3.SS2.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{\mathbf{y}}\!=\!M_{\theta}(\mathbf{x})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐲</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0.108em" rspace="0.108em">=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>M</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{\mathbf{y}}\!=\!M_{\theta}(\mathbf{x})</annotation></semantics></math> is the generated caption, <math id="S3.SS2.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M_{J}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>M</mi><mi>J</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M_{J}</annotation></semantics></math> is a frozen third-party judge model that answers <math id="S3.SS2.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{q}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝐪</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{q}</annotation></semantics></math> based on <math id="S3.SS2.p2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{\mathbf{y}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐲</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{\mathbf{y}}</annotation></semantics></math>, and <math id="S3.SS2.p2.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{I}(\cdot)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝕀</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{I}(\cdot)</annotation></semantics></math> is an indicator that returns <math id="S3.SS2.p2.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>1</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1</annotation></semantics></math> when the answer is correct.</p>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS2.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS2.p3.1" class="ltx_p">Obviously, the more diverse the query set <math id="S3.SS2.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{Q}_{\mathbf{x}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒬</mi><mi>𝐱</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{Q}_{\mathbf{x}}</annotation></semantics></math>, the more reliable the completeness reward becomes. Current methods, such as CapRL <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib9" title="" class="ltx_ref">53</a>]</cite>, generate queries using a single MLLM with simple prompts, which suffer from single-model bias and limited coverage. To alleviate this issue, we define a diversity <math id="S3.SS2.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{V}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{V}</annotation></semantics></math> over a query set <math id="S3.SS2.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{Q}_{\mathbf{x}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒬</mi><mi>𝐱</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{Q}_{\mathbf{x}}</annotation></semantics></math>:</p>
<table id="S3.E5" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.E5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{V}(\mathcal{Q}_{\mathbf{x}})=\frac{2}{m(m-1)}\sum_{i=1}^{m}\sum_{j&gt;i}\left(\frac{\mathbf{e_{i}}\cdot\mathbf{e_{j}}}{\|\mathbf{e_{i}}\|\|\mathbf{e_{j}}\|}-\bar{\mathbf{\mu}}\right)^{2}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒬</mi><mi>𝐱</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>2</mn><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>m</mi></munderover><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></munder><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>𝐞</mi><mi>𝐢</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msub><mi>𝐞</mi><mi>𝐣</mi></msub></mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mi>𝐞</mi><mi>𝐢</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mi>𝐞</mi><mi>𝐣</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac><mo>−</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>μ</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{V}(\mathcal{Q}_{\mathbf{x}})=\frac{2}{m(m-1)}\sum_{i=1}^{m}\sum_{j&gt;i}\left(\frac{\mathbf{e_{i}}\cdot\mathbf{e_{j}}}{\|\mathbf{e_{i}}\|\|\mathbf{e_{j}}\|}-\bar{\mathbf{\mu}}\right)^{2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(5)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.SS2.p3.2" class="ltx_p">where <math id="S3.SS2.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{e}_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝐞</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{e}_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> is the embedding vector of query <math id="S3.SS2.p3.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{q}_{i}\!\in\!\mathcal{Q}_{\mathbf{x}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝐪</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.108em" rspace="0.108em">∈</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒬</mi><mi>𝐱</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{q}_{i}\!\in\!\mathcal{Q}_{\mathbf{x}}</annotation></semantics></math>,
<math id="S3.SS2.p3.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>m</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m</annotation></semantics></math> represents the size of the query set, i.e., <math id="S3.SS2.p3.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m=|\mathcal{Q_{\mathbf{x}}}|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒬</mi><mi>𝐱</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m=|\mathcal{Q_{\mathbf{x}}}|</annotation></semantics></math>.
And <math id="S3.SS2.p3.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\small{\mathbf{\bar{\mu}}\!=\!\frac{2}{m(m-1)}\sum_{i=1}^{m}\sum_{j&gt;i}\frac{\mathbf{e_{i}}\cdot\mathbf{e_{j}}}{\|\mathbf{e_{i}}\|\|\mathbf{e_{j}}\|}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi mathsize="0.900em">μ</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo lspace="0.128em" mathsize="0.900em" rspace="0.128em">=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn mathsize="0.900em">2</mn><mrow><mi mathsize="0.900em">m</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">(</mo><mrow><mi mathsize="0.900em">m</mi><mo mathsize="0.900em">−</mo><mn mathsize="0.900em">1</mn></mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em" rspace="0em" stretchy="true">∑</mo><mrow><mi mathsize="0.900em">i</mi><mo mathsize="0.900em">=</mo><mn mathsize="0.900em">1</mn></mrow><mi mathsize="0.900em">m</mi></msubsup><mrow><msub><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em" stretchy="true">∑</mo><mrow><mi mathsize="0.900em">j</mi><mo mathsize="0.900em">&gt;</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">i</mi></mrow></msub><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi mathsize="0.900em">𝐞</mi><mi mathsize="0.900em">𝐢</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" mathsize="0.900em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msub><mi mathsize="0.900em">𝐞</mi><mi mathsize="0.900em">𝐣</mi></msub></mrow><mrow><mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em" stretchy="true">‖</mo><msub><mi mathsize="0.900em">𝐞</mi><mi mathsize="0.900em">𝐢</mi></msub><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em" stretchy="true">‖</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em" stretchy="true">‖</mo><msub><mi mathsize="0.900em">𝐞</mi><mi mathsize="0.900em">𝐣</mi></msub><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em" stretchy="true">‖</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\small{\mathbf{\bar{\mu}}\!=\!\frac{2}{m(m-1)}\sum_{i=1}^{m}\sum_{j&gt;i}\frac{\mathbf{e_{i}}\cdot\mathbf{e_{j}}}{\|\mathbf{e_{i}}\|\|\mathbf{e_{j}}\|}}</annotation></semantics></math>. Based on the diversity definition, we design a multi-MLLM query generation algorithm (as shown in Algorithm <a href="#alg1" title="Algorithm 1 ‣ 3.1 Preliminaries ‣ 3 Method ‣ CCCaption: Dual-Reward Reinforcement Learning for Complete and Correct Image Captioning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a>) that generates and filters queries using multiple MLLMs to promote query diversity and ensure completeness. Applying our algorithm to large-scale images yields a training set of 44k samples, with an average of 10 queries per image, denoted CCaption-44k.</p>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS2.p4" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S3.SS2.p4.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.SS2.p4.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Correctness Reward</span>. Building on prior work <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib15" title="" class="ltx_ref">56</a>, <a href="#bib.bib37" title="" class="ltx_ref">19</a>]</cite> on evaluating correctness,
we decompose the generated caption <math id="S3.SS2.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{\mathbf{y}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐲</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{\mathbf{y}}</annotation></semantics></math> into a set of sub-caption queries <math id="S3.SS2.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{Q}_{\hat{\mathbf{y}}}\!=\!\{\mathbf{q}_{i}\}_{i=1}^{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒬</mi><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐲</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></msub><mo lspace="0.108em" rspace="0.108em">=</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>𝐪</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{Q}_{\hat{\mathbf{y}}}\!=\!\{\mathbf{q}_{i}\}_{i=1}^{n}</annotation></semantics></math>, which serves as an approximation to the basic information set <math id="S3.SS2.p4.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{B}_{\mathbf{y}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℬ</mi><mi>𝐲</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{B}_{\mathbf{y}}</annotation></semantics></math>.
We then reward captions whose sub-caption queries are better grounded in the image.
Formally, the correctness reward is defined as</p>
<table id="S3.E6" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.E6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{R}_{\text{corr}}(\mathbf{x},\hat{\mathbf{y}})=\frac{1}{|\mathcal{Q}_{\hat{\mathbf{y}}}|}\sum_{\mathbf{q}\in\mathcal{Q}_{\hat{\mathbf{y}}}}M_{J}(\mathbf{x},\mathbf{q})," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℛ</mi><mtext>corr</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>,</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐲</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒬</mi><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐲</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>𝐪</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒬</mi><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐲</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></msub></mrow></munder><mrow><msub><mi>M</mi><mi>J</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝐪</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{R}_{\text{corr}}(\mathbf{x},\hat{\mathbf{y}})=\frac{1}{|\mathcal{Q}_{\hat{\mathbf{y}}}|}\sum_{\mathbf{q}\in\mathcal{Q}_{\hat{\mathbf{y}}}}M_{J}(\mathbf{x},\mathbf{q}),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(6)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.SS2.p4.2" class="ltx_p">where <math id="S3.SS2.p4.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M_{J}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>M</mi><mi>J</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M_{J}</annotation></semantics></math> is the same frozen third-party judge model, <math id="S3.SS2.p4.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M_{J}(\mathbf{x},\mathbf{q})\in[0,1]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>M</mi><mi>J</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝐪</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M_{J}(\mathbf{x},\mathbf{q})\in[0,1]</annotation></semantics></math> provides a soft assessment of how well each caption query is grounded given the image <math id="S3.SS2.p4.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{x}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝐱</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{x}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<figure id="S3.T1" class="ltx_table">
<div id="S3.T1.3" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_transformed_outer" style="width:2015.2pt;height:87.9pt;vertical-align:-41.7pt;"><span class="ltx_transformed_inner" style="transform:translate(-112.0pt,4.9pt) scale(0.9,0.9) ;">
<table id="S3.T1.3.1" class="ltx_tabular ltx_align_middle">
<tr id="S3.T1.3.1.1" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="S3.T1.3.1.1.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_r ltx_border_tt" style="padding-top:1pt;padding-bottom:1pt;" rowspan="2"><span id="S3.T1.3.1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text">MLLM</span></td>
<td id="S3.T1.3.1.1.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_border_tt" style="padding-top:1pt;padding-bottom:1pt;">
<span id="S3.T1.3.1.1.2.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top">
<span id="S3.T1.3.1.1.2.1.1" class="ltx_p ltx_align_center">Claude</span>
</span></td>
<td id="S3.T1.3.1.1.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_border_tt" style="padding-top:1pt;padding-bottom:1pt;">
